  "title": "bug: architectureRules lexer desync hides imports on later lines",
  "description": "extractImports in packages/moe-daemon/src/delivery/architectureRules.ts assumes a lexing misread stays on one line. That holds for strings and regexes, but not for template or `/* */` state. A regex/division misread, an Annex-B `<!--` comment, or a backtick in JSX text flips that state, so imports on LATER lines are hidden until the next backtick or `*/`. No uncertainty is reported.\n\nProbed on HEAD 7f04b869: every case below gives imports=[] and uncertain=[], and in a node vm Script the require in (1)-(3) really executes.\n1. `const a = {} / 1, b = `/;` NL `\\`;` NL require('../tools/t.js') NL `// \\``\n2. `class A extends /`/.constructor {}` NL require NL `// \\``\n3. `<!-- \\`` NL require NL `// \\``\n4. TSX `<p>Use \\` here</p>` NL require NL `// \\``\n5. `export default /\\/*/;` NL require NL `// */`\n6. `const r = a! / b; const p = `${x}/${y}`;` NL require NL `const q = \\`z\\`;`\n\nCases (4) and (6) can happen by accident.\n\nThis needs an architect decision. The V10a contract forbids adding an uncertainty reason, so the options are a new 'ambiguous' reason, parser-backed extraction, or something else. CQ-V10 must not trust 'passed' until this is resolved.\n\nFound in the CQ-V10a (task-2cd62d2c) step-5 adversarial review. Not fixed there, because its bytes are frozen under size waiver prop-7401cd0b.",
